     1	"""Kaggle episode archives -> ``kaggriculture-bc-shard-v1`` BC shards (Task 5.1).
     2	
     3	Lean preparation for the owner's BC data: every episode of the chosen days
     4	(default 2026-09-21..27), imitating one seat per episode, the winner by final
     5	bank (both seats on a draw).
     6	
     7	Input is a directory of day archives ``kaggriculture-episodes-YYYY-MM-DD.zip``
     8	whose members are ``<episode_id>.json`` Kaggle episodes. On the RunPod volume
     9	``4llk4uaf20`` that directory is
    10	``<mount>/kaggriculture-v2/public-episodes-2026-09-14-to-2026-09-27/archives``;
    11	the pod must confirm its actual mount path (``/workspace`` is the RunPod
    12	default, the historical reader used ``/data``).
    13	
    14	Per episode (one worker process each, one ZIP member in memory at a time):
    15	
    16	1. Envelope: 720 steps of two seats, ``info.EpisodeId`` equal to the member
    17	   name, an integer ``info.seed`` (custody only, never encoded), both final
    18	   statuses ``DONE``, the full Rust config key set.
    19	2. Winner seat(s) by final bank ``farms[s].money`` at the last step.
    20	3. For each kept turn ``t`` in ``0..718`` (all turns unless ``--turn-stride``),
    21	   the observation is ``steps[t]`` (seat 1's shared keys come from seat 0) and
    22	   the label of seat ``s`` is ``steps[t + 1][s].action``: Kaggle records the
    23	   action answering step ``t``'s observation at step ``t + 1``. The explicit
    24	   state header (placeholder seed 0) is encoded by the native Task 1.3 encoder
    25	   into both seat rows.
    26	4. Each policy seat's action is admitted strictly by the native Task 1.4 codec
    27	   (``kaggriculture_encode`` plus a decode round trip); falsy ``hands`` /
    28	   ``market`` values become ``[]`` as in the reference, counted by kind. A turn
    29	   is kept only if every policy seat is admitted; rejections are counted by
    30	   reason. The other seat row keeps its observation (the critic trains on both
    31	   outcomes) and carries an all-PASS placeholder program, which the trainer
    32	   never imitates (``policy_seat`` is false).
    33	5. The episode's split is a deterministic hash of its id (about
    34	   ``--validation-fraction``), and admitted rows go to one shard at
    35	   ``<split>/<day>-<episode_id>.npz`` through ``owl.kaggriculture.bc_data``.
    36	
    37	Every finished episode leaves ``records/<day>-<episode_id>.json``; a rerun
    38	skips those (resumable), and ``manifest.json`` is written once at the end.
    39	``records/identity.json`` binds the records to the source checkout, the
    40	label-affecting settings and every archive's SHA-256; a rerun whose identity
    41	differs fails instead of reusing stale labels or winners.
    42	Agent and team names are never read.
    43	
    44	``--pairing-sample N`` first steps N episodes through kaggle-environments' own
    45	Kaggriculture interpreter (with the recorded ``info.seed``) from every
    46	``steps[t]`` with ``steps[t + 1].action`` and counts how many transitions
    47	reproduce ``steps[t + 1]``: evidence for the step+1 pairing on this corpus.
    48	"""
