# Task 5.1 preparer r2 verification

Reviewed clean HEAD 356d19f6b3bd5a0e1102c674d96f5b71cabfb5e3 and git diff 49255ac 356d19f. No blocking findings. No tracked changes, pod access, downloads, GPU execution or training. All scratch artifacts are in this directory. Preparation tests execute the CPU preparer, not a learner.

## Resume identity

The actual CLI reproduction reuses the r1 two-episode payloads, copied into scratch archives exposed via seven scratch day-ZIP symlinks. Six archives are empty, as in r1; this tests the path/CLI and cached-record behavior, not the production corpus. The fresh run deliberately omits --days and records [22,23,24,25,26,27,28]. Both episodes are prepared with the original data, then manifest and the validation episode's record/shard are removed to model interruption. Same-input resume returns 0, reports 1 done / 1 to do, and preserves the cached train shard exactly.

After another simulated interruption, only the train episode's recorded terminal banks are exchanged in the scratch archive: [7213,42478] -> [42478,7213]. Resume returns 1 with RuntimeError: identity.json differs from this run in ['archive_sha256']. It never enters the cached-record loop, never publishes the pending record or manifest, and leaves the cached record and shard byte-identical. Removing identity.json also returns 1 with the explicit records-but-no-identity error. See resume-result.json, resume-repro.py and the per-invocation logs.

Source references: scripts/kaggriculture_prepare_bc.py:691 (clean checkout/head, locks, preparer and native-extension hashes); :738 (exact identity comparison and missing-identity rejection); :820 (archives of selected tasks hashed through symlinks); :824 (month/days/split/stride/hire limit/pairing binding); :855 (cached-record reuse after identity check).

No remaining label- or seat-affecting input was found unbound in the supported clean-checkout CLI path. Archive bytes bind recorded observations, actions, configuration and final banks. Clean revision identity, preparer hash and loaded native-extension hash bind the transformation. --resident-budget-gib is represented by the resulting turn_stride. --limit-episodes, worker count and pairing-sample size do not change an existing episode's labels or selected seats; limit changes episode selection. Hashes cover archives referenced by selected tasks; empty/unselected archives do not contribute records. The Python Kaggle interpreter is diagnostic only, not the source of training observations/actions.

## Defaults and static checks

scripts/kaggriculture_prepare_bc.py:772 defaults --days to 22-28, confirmed by actual CLI execution above. Mypy succeeds on both changed Python files. Ruff check succeeds and Ruff format --check reports both already formatted. The preparer pytest suite passes 21/21 in 3.96 seconds. git diff --check passes. Logs: mypy.log, ruff-direct.log, ruff-format.log, pytest.log. The first uvx invocation was prevented from creating a tools-directory temp file; the installed ruff binary then completed successfully without downloading anything.

## Pod evidence interpretation

The supplied 5743/5752 result is not a full transition-parity pass. All reported mismatch turns satisfy (t+1)%24 == 0. In the pinned kaggle-environments 1.32.7 interpreter, line 945 triggers _end_of_day. Lines 843-857 deposit carried inventory into the shed in dict iteration order, discard overflow, and lines 878-882 reset inventory. This is the likely location of a private-only day-boundary discrepancy.

A plausible concrete cause is loss of live dictionary insertion order during JSON export: core.py:409-410 uses sort_keys=True. With one free shed slot, carried WHEAT then CARROT preserves WHEAT; sorted-JSON reload preserves CARROT instead. private-order-probe.py calls the actual pinned helper and demonstrates this private-only difference; private-order-probe.json records outputs and interpreter SHA-256 bc8a54879ef02c7ea64b8b333d6a976f0ea65c4949149d01f463f23bccee653e (same as r1). This is a demonstrated mechanism, not proof of these nine exact episodes' export path or differing fields, which were not available locally.

The proposed hidden/private RNG explanation is unsupported by this source. kaggriculture.py:869-871 reconstructs RNG from the recorded seed and day every day; its consumers at :877 and :891 change public weeds/shops. scripts/kaggriculture_prepare_bc.py:523 supplies that seed. No carried RNG state is required here.

